## [Agent Activity Logging (GitHub Projects Integration)]
- **One Ticket Per Agent (Strict):** Each agent (0~6) MUST create its OWN separate GitHub Issue for its own work. Do NOT bundle multiple agents into a single issue.
- **Mandatory Pre-Action Ticket Creation:** BEFORE executing any task, the agent MUST create a GitHub Issue using the GitHub CLI (`gh issue create`).
  - The issue body MUST include `Start Date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM KST`
- **Mandatory Completion Status (Close & Comment):** AFTER the action is complete, the agent MUST:
  1. Add a completion comment: `gh issue comment <url> --body "완료 요약: ..."`
  2. Close the issue: `gh issue close <url>`
- **Feature Branch Per Agent:** Each agent MUST work on its own feature branch:
  - Branch format: `agent/<role>/<short-description>` (e.g., `agent/image/mars-cards`)
  - Create branch: `git checkout -b agent/<role>/<short-description>`
  - Commit only the agent's own files, then push the branch.
- **Pull Request & Link:** After pushing the branch, the agent MUST create a PR and link it to the issue:
  - `gh pr create --title "..." --body "Closes #<issue-number>" --head <branch>`
  - The issue body must reference the PR once created: add a comment `gh issue comment <url> --body "PR: <pr-url>"`
- **Agent-Scoped Commits:** Each agent pushes ONLY its own changed files. Do NOT mix files from different agents in one commit.
- **GitHub CLI Command (Creation):**
  ```
  gh issue create --repo jowa131/c4c \
    --title "[{role} agent] {Short Task Summary}" \
    --body "Start Date: {YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM KST}\n\n{Detailed Action Plan}"
  ```
- **Agent Identity Format (Strictly No Emojis):** Use plain English agent roles:
  - content agent
  - planner agent
  - developer agent
  - image agent
  - review agent
  - devops agent
  - data/cx agent
